1
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,289 --> 00:01:37,740
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:40,509
These are three human lives,

4
00:01:40,509 --> 00:01:40,950
Mei.

5
00:01:41,229 --> 00:01:42,630
How come there are three?

6
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,060
If he's convicted,

7
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,039
Qian Xingliang
will definitely get the death penalty.

8
00:01:46,039 --> 00:01:47,400
Then who exactly is the deceased?

9
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,509
We don't even know whether Yu Sanhua

10
00:01:48,509 --> 00:01:49,680
is dead or not.

11
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:57,789
Xia.

12
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:01,870
This case

13
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,950
is a decent one I finally got

14
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,710
after enduring things here

15
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:06,710
for three years.

16
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,400
I value it

17
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:09,840
very highly.

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,710
I know.

19
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,590
That's why I'm eagerer to help you.

20
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:15,650
How can you help me?

21
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,800
By asking me to return the files?

22
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:30,470
The difference between us now

23
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:31,200
is too great.

24
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,400
We also won't be able to
try it well in court,

25
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,470
and we may even make a fool of ourselves.

26
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:37,329
How about this?

27
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,360
Go find the chief judge,

28
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,520
the court president or other superiors.

29
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,400
Let them decide

30
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,520
which of us will stay or leave.

31
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,120
As long as the leaders say it,

32
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,120
I'll obey unconditionally.

33
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,590
Mei.

34
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,560
It doesn't have to be either of us leaving

35
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,630
or staying here, does it?

36
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:51,360
Yes, it does.

37
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,750
That is a way to show full respect

38
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:54,680
for both of us.

39
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,880
Are you going or not?

40
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:01,150
If you're not going, I will.

41
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:02,310
Fine.

42
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,310
I'll go.

43
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:09,870
Yu.

44
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,000
I think

45
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:14,800
this case

46
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,190
should be handled according to the files

47
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:17,680
sent by the procuratorate.

48
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,680
Let's not complicate the matters.

49
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,340
Court Pres.

50
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,210
I understand what you mean.

51
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:22,840
I quite appreciate your sense

52
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,590
of justice.

53
00:03:24,430 --> 00:03:24,910
But...

54
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:25,340
Court Pres.,

55
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,120
let's put aside the sense of justice

56
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,910
and just talk about
the realistic problems.

57
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:29,360
Okay.

58
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:31,490
If we leave room for flexibility

59
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:32,490
in this case,

60
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,840
not only will it fail to
solve the public-opinion issue,

61
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:37,100
but it will also bring us hidden dangers.

62
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:38,240
As for Song Xiaoguang's

63
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,520
disguise of mental illness,

64
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,800
anyone with a discerning eye
can sense it instantly.

65
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,310
If we back down now,

66
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:44,470
people outside will all gossip about

67
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:47,130
how powerful men
can gain everything they want.

68
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,450
But Court Pres.,

69
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:49,870
if we handle it strictly,

70
00:03:50,329 --> 00:03:51,520
not only can we preserve

71
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,329
the reputation of our Intermediate Court,

72
00:03:53,329 --> 00:03:54,770
but we can also

73
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,840
set a standard for

74
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,610
similar related cases.

75
00:03:57,690 --> 00:03:58,400
If things go well,

76
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,380
it's naturally due to your

77
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,360
excellent leadership
as the court president.

78
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,240
If it doesn't go well...

79
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:02,910
Don't worry.

80
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:03,680
I will ensure that

81
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,120
everything is signed and documented.

82
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,290
If the superiors hold us accountable,

83
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:07,910
I will be the first to step forward.

84
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:08,570
Court Pres.

85
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,030
In short,

86
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,240
if we succeed,
we'll be heroes upholding justice.

87
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,120
If we release

88
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:15,520
that maniac now,

89
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:16,750
you will inevitably have to

90
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,209
clean up their mess later.

91
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,829
What do you mean by cleaning up a mess?

92
00:04:20,829 --> 00:04:21,890
Be more civilized.

93
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:27,240
What you said

94
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,880
does make some sense.

95
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:30,750
However,

96
00:04:31,050 --> 00:04:31,900
if we openly challenge

97
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,980
this matter now,

98
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,450
wouldn't it be inappropriate?

99
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,270
It's certainly good to be able to

100
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:41,630
analyze the situation

101
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:43,240
and have political sensitivity.

102
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:43,940
But if there are

103
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:44,800
no good solutions,

104
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:45,270
then...

105
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,220
Court Pres.

106
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,270
There is actually a solution.

107
00:04:48,270 --> 00:04:50,470
Otherwise, I wouldn't have come to you.

108
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:55,909
Yu.

109
00:04:57,070 --> 00:04:58,330
How many years have you

110
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,520
been working here?

111
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,520
Over three years.

112
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,240
Then tell me

113
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:05,270
what the solution is.

114
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:07,720
Okay.

115
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,990
These are really good today.

116
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:12,390
-The filling is good.
-Yummy.

117
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:12,920
Taste it.

118
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:14,770
Lihui.

119
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,720
What are your plans next?

120
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:19,240
Won't you consider getting a Ph.D.?

121
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:20,950
I only want to apply
to be your doctoral student.

122
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:21,950
Is that okay, sir?

123
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,240
That's great.

124
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:25,670
You are welcome to apply.

125
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,270
Hey, cheers.

126
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:26,730
Cheers.

127
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,470
It's a deal.

128
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,900
But, Lihui,

129
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,940
I have a small suggestion.

130
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,080
If you study for a Ph.D.,

131
00:05:38,190 --> 00:05:40,190
you shouldn't work at the same time.

132
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,700
I'm afraid I still have to.

133
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:44,070
What's more, it'll take a few years

134
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:46,130
before I come back to get a doctorate.

135
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,360
That's fine, too.

136
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:49,090
Why is that?

137
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:51,520
Do you have a boyfriend?

138
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:53,600
No.

139
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,260
I'm being transferred to another place.

140
00:05:57,159 --> 00:05:58,070
Where will you go?

141
00:05:58,070 --> 00:05:58,800
In a few days,

142
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:00,380
I'll go to the Xijiang Procuratorate

143
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,440
to report for duty.

144
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:08,310
That's good, too.

145
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,680
Getting experience
in a provincial procuratorate

146
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,610
is not a bad idea.

147
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:15,510
It's an even lower-level institution.

148
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:17,000
I'll go to Bieshan Prison

149
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,600
to be a resident prosecutor.

150
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:20,560
Where?

151
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:23,680
Prison?

152
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:26,280
Whose idea is this?

153
00:06:27,070 --> 00:06:27,800
Who decided this?

154
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,000
Isn't this so wicked?

155
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:29,890
As a girl,

156
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,920
why are you going to work in a prison?

157
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,000
Zhou.

158
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,210
Aren't they all your students?

159
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,680
For example, that person

160
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,540
and so-and-so.

161
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:38,830
Go ask them.

162
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,159
What mistake did Lihui make?

163
00:06:41,159 --> 00:06:42,280
Why are they exiling Lihui like this?

164
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,240
I'm not being exiled.

165
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,070
Ma'am, I requested it myself.

166
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,460
Have you suffered any injustice?

167
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,360
It has nothing to do with anyone.

168
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,920
I decided it myself.

169
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,260
Then tell us your reasons.

170
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:00,990
My reasons

171
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,160
are not that complicated.

172
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,190
I just feel that

173
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,390
once I graduated,

174
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:07,160
I went to work
at the Supreme People's Procuratorate,

175
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,560
so I've had
no practical experience at all.

176
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,750
I didn't think much of it
in the first few years.

177
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:13,390
But in the past two years,
I've found it more and more

178
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:15,790
necessary to make up for
my missed lessons.

179
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:17,870
But there's no need to go so far.

180
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:19,480
Ma'am,

181
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,330
since I'm going to
a grassroots institution,

182
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:22,630
I'd better go to the lowest-level one.

183
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:23,560
Silly child.

184
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:27,020
You're thinking of it too simply.

185
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:28,480
If you go so far,

186
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:30,840
can you still come back?

187
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:34,720
I haven't thought about that.

188
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:35,310
Lihui,

189
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,780
you can't act wilfully like this.

190
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:41,430
M-Ma'am, please don't be like this.

191
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,680
Alright. Let's eat.

192
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,920
Good, good, good!

193
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:55,970
Good!

194
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,090
Run! Run!

195
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:57,650
Come on!

196
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:59,670
Let your feet move more agilely.

197
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:14,630
What?

198
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,050
Are you here specifically to thank me?

199
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,070
Not specifically.

200
00:08:19,070 --> 00:08:21,430
I just want to thank you
for helping me last time.

201
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:23,340
There are also many questions
I haven't asked.

202
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,720
I think I can ask you again this time

203
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,390
when I'm here.

204
00:08:25,390 --> 00:08:27,390
But they're unrelated to that case.

205
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:29,010
Do I have to answer?

206
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,600
I don't care. I'm asking.

207
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,770
Here's the first question.

208
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:37,730
Has your leg been like this

209
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,159
since kindergarten?

210
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,750
Last time, when a person asked me that,

211
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:43,600
I took a glass of water

212
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,510
and pour it on his face.

213
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:46,080
You know I mean no harm.

214
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,540
Polio.

215
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,810
It's been like this since I was three.

216
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:55,230
Here's the second question.

217
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,360
Do you sit here every day

218
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,160
watching them play basketball?

219
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,630
I'm their coach.

220
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,970
You're their coach?

221
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,870
Even though I can't even shoot a ball,

222
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:09,130
I understand tactics.

223
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:10,640
What's more, I would encourage them.

224
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,840
They all listen to me.

225
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,640
Our team has no rival

226
00:09:13,670 --> 00:09:15,070
in the nearby compounds.

227
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,480
You can play basketball too, right?

228
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,280
You saw it last time, didn't you?

229
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,240
I was the captain

230
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,320
of our school team,

231
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:26,170
the President of the Student Union

232
00:09:26,550 --> 00:09:27,210
and a cadre.

233
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,140
I'm the chosen one.

234
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:31,910
That's impressive, huh?

235
00:09:32,650 --> 00:09:33,600
Then why were you assigned

236
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,130
to this small place of ours?

237
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,320
Did you make a huge mistake?

238
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,240
There was something fishy
about the assigning process?

239
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,270
I may not know about other things,

240
00:09:40,270 --> 00:09:40,960
but I have

241
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,780
a good political background.

242
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:49,280
Let's go.

243
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,650
Let's play basketball.

244
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,150
Let's play basketball!

245
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:54,810
Be careful.

246
00:09:56,870 --> 00:09:57,840
What?

247
00:09:58,870 --> 00:09:59,600
Give it to me.

248
00:10:10,270 --> 00:10:10,750
Try it.

249
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,080
Just hold it like this.

250
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,340
When you shoot, use this hand

251
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:13,810
to support it.

252
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:15,240
Then do it like this. Bend your arm.

253
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,150
When you use your strength in the end,

254
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:17,720
press it with your middle three fingers.

255
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,450
Give it a try.

256
00:10:19,270 --> 00:10:20,000
Then I'll do this now.

257
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,870
Come on! Come on! Come on!

258
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:28,680
It's fine.

259
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,480
It's actually very good
for your first time.

260
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,810
No rush. Take your time.

261
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:35,840
No rush. Take your time.

262
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,360
Come on!

263
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:38,120
I'm doing it!

264
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:40,390
Come on! Come on! Come on!

265
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,500
I almost made the shot.

266
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:43,940
Try again.

267
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:46,600
Come on!

268
00:10:57,910 --> 00:10:58,510
Lihui.

269
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,870
While making major life decisions,

270
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:02,200
you might be impulsive.

271
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,830
But you mustn't act out of spite.

272
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,440
Sir.

273
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:09,010
I'm not acting out of spite.

274
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:11,770
I'm just not very satisfied with myself.

275
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:14,750
The more I try to maintain
my dignity on the surface,

276
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:16,080
the more it makes me look

277
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:18,910
weak and hypocritical.

278
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:24,630
Sir,

279
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,050
don't worry.

280
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,330
I've made this decision

281
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:31,320
not because I want to put on

282
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,720
a tragic play for myself.

283
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,270
I genuinely

284
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,860
want to change myself.

285
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,120
Alright then.

286
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:39,550
I'll support you.

287
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,260
I have always felt that

288
00:11:44,630 --> 00:11:46,910
judges and prosecutors

289
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:49,030
should be the professions

290
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:51,360
with the highest thresholds in the world.

291
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:54,500
Because they have to judge and decide

292
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,460
other people's lives.

293
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,600
If a person doesn't have
an independent personality

294
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,130
and always feels inferior,

295
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:03,440
he indeed can't

296
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,150
become a qualified judge

297
00:12:06,030 --> 00:12:06,890
or prosecutor.

298
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,560
The meaning and value

299
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,750
of our work

300
00:12:10,570 --> 00:12:11,290
is to protect

301
00:12:11,290 --> 00:12:14,220
the lives and dignity
of those ordinary individuals

302
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,630
and to promote goodness
for the entire society.

303
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:18,490
Think about it.

304
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:20,960
Is there anything

305
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,370
more meaningful than this?

306
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,000
I will definitely become

307
00:12:26,510 --> 00:12:28,640
the kind of person you mentioned, sir.

308
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:30,970
Definitely.

309
00:12:48,870 --> 00:13:00,000
[Beijing Station]

310
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,040
Dear passengers,

311
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:52,630
welcome to Beijing Railway Station.

312
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:55,080
Our station is dedicated to providing

313
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,750
good travel services for all passengers.

314
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,910
Please comply with the station's rules
and regulations

315
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:00,640
while waiting for your trains.

316
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:16,010
I need to make a phone call.

317
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:18,200
One yuan if they call back,
30 cents if they don't.

318
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:18,530
Okay.

319
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,770
Hello, page 0487. My surname is Yu.

320
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,540
It's urgent. Please call back immediately.

321
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:31,600
Sir.

322
00:13:31,630 --> 00:13:32,360
Is there any place nearby

323
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:35,020
that's suitable
for treating someone to a meal?

324
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:35,720
Yes.

325
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:37,520
See the one up there?

326
00:13:37,670 --> 00:13:38,510
It provides Cantonese food

327
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:39,630
and fresh seafood.

328
00:13:39,630 --> 00:13:39,960
I'll leave the money here.

329
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,550
It's very classy. I'm telling you.

330
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:42,810
Just one lobster there

331
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:44,360
costs as much as what I earn
by selling newspapers for three months.

332
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,080
Are there any places
that are more affordable?

333
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,910
Young man,
if you're trying to get things done,

334
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,770
Cantonese food is the classiest.

335
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,770
Okay. I'll be waiting for a call.

336
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:53,600
Tell me when they call back.

337
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,360
I'm right around here.

338
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:54,690
Okay.

339
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,480
As for this steamed fish,

340
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,360
could you get a smaller one for me?

341
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,600
I'm sorry, sir.

342
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,460
The smallest fish we have here

343
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:02,720
is over 1.5 kilograms.

344
00:14:02,770 --> 00:14:04,080
But the two of us
can't eat up a 1.5-kilograms fish.

345
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,240
That's enough. Don't order it.

346
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,240
I don't like fish.

347
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,270
What about the wine?
What wine should we drink?

348
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:09,800
This one.

349
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,520
Stop looking at this.

350
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,510
I can't drink.
I have to work this afternoon.

351
00:14:13,510 --> 00:14:13,920
Okay.

352
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:15,020
Alright. That's all for now.

353
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:15,340
Okay.

354
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:16,270
Okay. Thank you.

355
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,240
Yu Gaoyuan.

356
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:29,390
This meal
will cost you several hundred yuan.

357
00:14:29,390 --> 00:14:30,240
What's wrong with you?

358
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,960
Aren't you going to live your life?

359
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:32,870
When treating someone to a meal,

360
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:34,400
shouldn't I do it properly?

361
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,570
I've even brought my bankbook.

362
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:37,920
Have some tea.

363
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:44,120
Chief Judge.

364
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,150
She's not even as good as Sun.

365
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,010
Whatever she says is right,

366
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:49,680
and whatever I say is wrong.

367
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,790
On what grounds could she do this?

368
00:14:51,790 --> 00:14:52,320
Just because she graduated

369
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,030
from a prestigious university?

370
00:14:54,030 --> 00:14:56,720
But I graduated from Dongdu University
of Political Science and Law, too.

371
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,450
Chief Judge,

372
00:14:57,510 --> 00:14:59,630
didn't you also graduate from that school?

373
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:00,430
Yes, yes, yes.

374
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:02,670
Anyway, regarding this case,

375
00:15:02,670 --> 00:15:04,730
I definitely won't return the files.

376
00:15:05,550 --> 00:15:06,080
Xia.

377
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:07,940
Why are you standing here?

378
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:09,170
Nothing, nothing.

379
00:15:30,270 --> 00:15:31,630
There's a misunderstanding between us.

380
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:32,960
Let's clear it up today.

381
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,120
What happened between Lihui and me

382
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:38,910
wasn't really like...

383
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:40,710
Alright. Stop talking about it.

384
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,850
It has nothing to do with me indeed.

385
00:15:44,850 --> 00:15:46,210
But as a lawyer,

386
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:46,650
I more or less

387
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:48,010
have a sense of justice.

388
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:50,910
What's more, it's all in the past.

389
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:51,720
When I said
I'd cut ties with you that day,

390
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,250
it was just liquor talking.

391
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:54,630
Okay.

392
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:03,480
Zhang Lihui is not
at the Supreme People's Procuratorate.

393
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,920
She went to Xijiang. Do you know that?

394
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:05,360
What happened?

395
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,750
I really didn't know about this.

396
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,050
Is it because of what happened before?

397
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,340
Do you think you're so important?

398
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:11,160
Why does everyone
have to be connected to you?

399
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,120
Can't she have her own

400
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:12,920
aspirations?

401
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,050
Yes, she can.

402
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,070
Why are you...

403
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:23,090
Are you here this time

404
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:25,550
specifically to see me
and treat me to a meal?

405
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:27,410
I'm here specifically to see you.

406
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,030
I need your help

407
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:31,870
with a case.

408
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,600
Yu Gaoyuan, what's wrong with you?

409
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,860
Do you want to quit wearing this uniform?

410
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,480
I think you need to continue to

411
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,940
participate in this case.

412
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:48,870
But right now,

413
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:50,870
my conflict with Mei has escalated.

414
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:51,550
She couldn't wait anymore

415
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:52,690
and just went to
see the chief judge herself.

416
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:54,290
She probably wants to
transfer me away from here.

417
00:16:54,290 --> 00:16:55,720
Then don't escalate the conflict.

418
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,690
Just compromise with her

419
00:16:56,690 --> 00:16:57,720
and say some nice things to her.

420
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,850
Why should I do that?

421
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,120
Are you insisting because you believe

422
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:01,850
she's wrong,

423
00:17:01,910 --> 00:17:02,960
or you think it's a life-and-death matter,

424
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,359
so you can't be careless?

425
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:06,640
To be honest,

426
00:17:07,589 --> 00:17:08,550
both are the reasons.

427
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:10,640
If you want to prove she's wrong,

428
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:13,200
it doesn't matter if you quit.

429
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:13,680
Because this matter

430
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,030
is actually meaningless.

431
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:16,440
What's more, whether she's right or not

432
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,550
is not for you to decide.

433
00:17:17,550 --> 00:17:18,680
Only time will tell.

434
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:20,890
Maybe in the end,

435
00:17:21,030 --> 00:17:21,750
she's not wrong at all,

436
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:23,200
and you just overthought it.

437
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,060
I think you've misunderstood me.

438
00:17:25,369 --> 00:17:27,000
It's precisely because
I don't know the answer

439
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,960
that I don't want to
treat human lives carelessly.

440
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,160
If you don't want to
treat human lives carelessly,

441
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,550
you have do everything you can

442
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:34,200
to continue to participate in this case.

443
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:36,240
Currently, criminal trials in China

444
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,830
are still investigation-centered.

445
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:39,120
If there are unresolved issues

446
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,110
during the investigation stage,

447
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:41,480
it is basically impossible
for you to rely on

448
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:43,480
the presiding judge to turn the tide

449
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,880
in court.

450
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:46,790
Moreover, that wouldn't be

451
00:17:46,790 --> 00:17:48,050
fair to the litigants.

452
00:17:48,350 --> 00:17:49,480
It's too dangerous.

453
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:51,850
As for this case,

454
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:54,170
Qian Xingliang

455
00:17:54,310 --> 00:17:55,840
needs to find a good lawyer.

456
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,260
He does have an appointed lawyer now.

457
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:01,880
In this kind of case,

458
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,260
do you think an appointed lawyer

459
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:04,150
can help?

460
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,170
I don't know.

461
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:14,480
If you want to continue to
participate in the case,

462
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,240
listen to me.

463
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,900
Go back and apologize to her,

464
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:20,160
even if you have to
say some hypocritical words.

465
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:20,590
Well,

466
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:23,510
everyone knows the tricks
of playing along.

467
00:18:23,510 --> 00:18:25,550
I'm just usually unwilling to fake it.

468
00:18:25,550 --> 00:18:27,150
You're unwilling to fake it?

469
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:29,270
You...

470
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:31,550
don't have to fake it in front of me.

471
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:31,960
You...

472
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,210
Why don't you practice first?

473
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:37,000
Just practice with me.

474
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,110
Say some...

475
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:40,440
Say some hypocritical words

476
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,240
that you normally wouldn't say.

477
00:18:43,550 --> 00:18:44,210
Let's do it.

478
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:47,210
Let's do it.

479
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:49,920
W-What should I say?

480
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,920
Just pretend this is...

481
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:58,270
a date for us today.

482
00:18:58,270 --> 00:18:59,400
And you're going to
confess your love to me.

483
00:18:59,400 --> 00:18:59,930
Go ahead.

484
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,320
You can't even say a word?

485
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:16,280
So childish.

486
00:19:31,350 --> 00:19:31,920
Got it.

487
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:35,960
To catch the prime culprit,
Song Xiaoguang,

488
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:38,480
you need to find a lawyer
who dares to speak out

489
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,030
to defend those minions,

490
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,900
voice grievances for them

491
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,260
and complain about unfair verdicts.

492
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:44,640
Only then can you guys legitimately

493
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,440
propose a re-appraisal, right?

494
00:19:46,590 --> 00:19:47,590
Good for you.

495
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:49,270
This is what you're like indeed.

496
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:50,730
What a smart calculation.

497
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:55,590
By setting a trap for Song Xiaoguang

498
00:19:55,590 --> 00:19:56,790
and using us as a tool,

499
00:19:57,050 --> 00:19:58,510
you guys will offend no one

500
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,680
and take all the benefits

501
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,640
with no risks at all.

502
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:01,790
If Song Xiaoguang is convicted,

503
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:04,730
you'll be the righteous judge
upholding justice for the people.

504
00:20:04,730 --> 00:20:05,720
What if we lose the lawsuit?

505
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,180
Even if you lose the lawsuit,

506
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:07,360
won't you still get the attorney's fees?

507
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,220
Give me a break.

508
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:11,000
You think Mr. Yuan is working for charity?

509
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:11,750
To handle a case like this,

510
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,680
we won't even earn enough
to pay for this meal.

511
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:14,280
Then what?

512
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,110
Do you agree to let Mr. Yuan handle it?

513
00:20:17,110 --> 00:20:17,720
No.

514
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,680
Wait a moment.

515
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:26,400
You...

516
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,880
How much is the attorney's fee

517
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,010
you just mentioned?

518
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,540
I've asked around.

519
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:33,520
The family member

520
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,440
of one of the victims

521
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,440
is a businessman.

522
00:20:35,870 --> 00:20:36,960
They are quite well-off

523
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,490
and can offer a lot of money.

524
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:39,920
His daughter was ruined by Song Xiaoguang

525
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:43,110
and eventually committed suicide
by jumping into the river.

526
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:43,680
I...

527
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,970
We're not doing this for money.

528
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,030
Sometimes justice is quite expensive.

529
00:20:50,030 --> 00:20:50,430
Right?

530
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:53,120
We lawyers need to make a living too,
don't we?

531
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:54,790
Let me tell you.

532
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,880
This case has already

533
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:57,960
gone to trial.

534
00:20:58,920 --> 00:20:59,510
Those accomplices

535
00:20:59,510 --> 00:21:01,110
have their own defense lawyers.

536
00:21:01,110 --> 00:21:02,510
If they want to
change their defense lawyers,

537
00:21:02,510 --> 00:21:03,750
it'll be a bit difficult.

538
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,130
But it's not impossible.

539
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:05,880
If you guys want to

540
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:06,570
take this case,

541
00:21:06,570 --> 00:21:07,310
you'll have to start from

542
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:08,940
the civil compensation for the victims

543
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,470
and use it as an entry point.

544
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,280
You've thought this all out.

545
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:14,400
This meal of yours

546
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,530
isn't a waste at all.

547
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,030
I was on the train for two days.

548
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:18,750
It took me more than 10 hours.

549
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:19,700
I had to stand for over 10 hours.

550
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:20,520
I'm going back tonight.

551
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:21,400
If I can't get anything out of this chat,

552
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,880
wouldn't this trip be in vain?

553
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,030
Why are you in such a hurry?

554
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:25,070
Aren't you going to visit Mr. Cheng

555
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:25,800
and Mr. Zhou?

556
00:21:26,270 --> 00:21:27,390
They usually pay a lot of attention
to you.

557
00:21:27,390 --> 00:21:28,310
What is it about me
they'd pay attention to?

558
00:21:28,310 --> 00:21:29,370
It would be fine
as long as they don't laugh at me.

559
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:30,760
They would pay attention to me?

560
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:31,550
What? Shall I go over there

561
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:32,590
and say, "Thank you both

562
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:33,920
for assigning me to Binjiang"?

563
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:35,740
What you're thinking is too extreme.

564
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:37,000
Even if they had not
assigned you to Binjiang

565
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,720
and had assigned you
to the Supreme People's Court

566
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:39,690
or the Supreme People's Procuratorate,

567
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:40,240
what would you do then?

568
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,130
W-Would you be able to take on

569
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:41,990
such a big case?

570
00:21:43,410 --> 00:21:44,680
My parents will go to Binjiang
in a couple of days,

571
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:46,680
so I need to go back there in advance.

572
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:51,280
Lu,

573
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:53,900
put aside
your personal prejudice against me.

574
00:21:54,070 --> 00:21:54,640
In this case,

575
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,770
no matter how I plot,

576
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:58,350
eventually, my purpose
is still to arrest Song Xiaoguang

577
00:21:58,350 --> 00:22:00,030
and put him in the dock.

578
00:22:02,270 --> 00:22:02,920
As for other things,

579
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,400
I don't care what you say about me.

580
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,460
There aren't many people I can trust.

581
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,070
You are one of those I trust,

582
00:22:08,070 --> 00:22:09,400
and Mr. Yuan is another.

583
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:11,190
Why do you trust me?

584
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:12,260
I stink of money.

585
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:13,830
I don't care
whether you stink of money or not.

586
00:22:13,830 --> 00:22:14,690
Li Xiang's case

587
00:22:15,630 --> 00:22:17,090
has always been in my mind.

588
00:22:21,750 --> 00:22:22,970
So you're done eating?

589
00:22:22,970 --> 00:22:23,500
I'm full.

590
00:22:24,270 --> 00:22:25,730
Waiter, the bill, please.

591
00:22:25,790 --> 00:22:26,250
Coming.

592
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:28,690
How much?

593
00:22:29,690 --> 00:22:31,010
136 yuan in total.

594
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:32,000
136 yuan.

595
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:34,830
136 yuan.

596
00:22:39,750 --> 00:22:40,110
Here.

597
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:40,830
Okay.

598
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:44,040
I've noticed that your wallet
is made of leather.

599
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:51,730
♪ I'll hold your hand tightly, my friend ♪

600
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,960
♪ The night sky is far away ♪

601
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:55,980
♪ Looking at the starlight,
we are closely connected ♪

602
00:22:56,010 --> 00:23:01,120
♪ Even if there would be thorns
all over the roads ahead ♪

603
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:05,650
♪ Untie the loneliness in my heart ♪

604
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:09,460
♪ Who can understand me? ♪

605
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:11,290
♪ We're like hands ♪

606
00:23:11,310 --> 00:23:13,690
♪ Being happy and sad together ♪

607
00:23:13,710 --> 00:23:18,920
♪ And we always share the burden ♪

608
00:23:14,270 --> 00:23:14,800
Alright.

609
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:19,720
I'll be waiting for your messages.

610
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:21,940
♪ You would do anything for me ♪

611
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:24,220
♪ I would do anything for you ♪

612
00:23:24,910 --> 00:23:27,670
♪ When we face difficulties
in despair together ♪

613
00:23:27,690 --> 00:23:37,090
♪ I'll hold your hand tightly, my friend ♪

614
00:23:40,590 --> 00:23:41,160
Sir.

615
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:42,940
The gentleman in the suit

616
00:23:42,940 --> 00:23:44,310
already paid the bill just now.

617
00:23:44,310 --> 00:23:45,770
I'm returning this to you.

618
00:23:48,530 --> 00:23:49,960
Please pack the food for me.

619
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:50,290
Okay.

620
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,160
I'm leaving now.

621
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:23,490
Okay.

622
00:24:24,750 --> 00:24:25,210
Come on.

623
00:24:25,550 --> 00:24:26,080
Be quick.

624
00:24:26,450 --> 00:24:27,480
Buns, rice and steamed bread.

625
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:28,480
We have everything.

626
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:29,740
Freshly steamed buns.

627
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:42,480
Sun.

628
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:44,720
Prosecutor Chen.

629
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:45,140
Here.

630
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:46,480
Have a pancake.

631
00:24:46,510 --> 00:24:48,570
How come his restaurant is reopened?

632
00:24:48,590 --> 00:24:50,680
His brother-in-law
took over the restaurant.

633
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,210
Taste it.

634
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:53,120
I'm really not eating it.

635
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:54,550
Then you can also reopen your restaurant.

636
00:24:54,550 --> 00:24:56,480
Why are you setting up a stall here?

637
00:24:57,220 --> 00:24:59,020
I don't have the energy for that.

638
00:24:59,440 --> 00:25:00,970
My family is in such a state.

639
00:25:01,510 --> 00:25:03,510
And I don't have the capital, either.

640
00:25:03,510 --> 00:25:04,070
Taste it.

641
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,200
Today, I'm here

642
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:07,130
because of this.

643
00:25:07,790 --> 00:25:09,070
People in our workplace

644
00:25:09,070 --> 00:25:10,200
chipped in some money.

645
00:25:10,200 --> 00:25:11,790
All the details are inside here.

646
00:25:11,790 --> 00:25:12,720
Take this for now

647
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,380
to treat your wife's illness.

648
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:18,150
Freshly steamed buns. They smell great.

649
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:18,820
No, no.

650
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:20,250
I can't take this money.

651
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,610
I only have one request for you.

652
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,640
Hurry up and bring them to trial.

653
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,000
Give them a severe sentence soon,

654
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,260
and I'll be satisfied.

655
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,240
I understand.

656
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,580
But treating your wife's illness
is more important.

657
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:30,350
Don't worry about anything else for now.

658
00:25:30,350 --> 00:25:31,270
-Okay?
-No, no, no.

659
00:25:31,270 --> 00:25:31,830
Dad!

660
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,040
What's wrong?

661
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:35,480
My mom is missing.

662
00:25:54,790 --> 00:25:55,790
Where is your mom?

663
00:26:01,550 --> 00:26:02,880
You didn't use the rope.

664
00:26:03,310 --> 00:26:04,530
What do I need you for?

665
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,620
Why are you hitting the child?

666
00:26:07,790 --> 00:26:08,250
Tell me.

667
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:09,270
Tell me!

668
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,810
I noticed that she was suffering too much.

669
00:26:12,810 --> 00:26:15,110
Being tied up with a rope,
she was in great pain.

670
00:26:15,110 --> 00:26:16,480
Didn't I know she was in pain?

671
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:17,030
Alright, alright!

672
00:26:17,030 --> 00:26:17,310
I...

673
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,270
-Now just think about...
-I...

674
00:26:18,270 --> 00:26:19,750
Now just think about
where your wife might be.

675
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:20,210
Okay?

676
00:26:20,550 --> 00:26:22,150
How would I know where she is?

677
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:23,510
I... I...

678
00:26:24,830 --> 00:26:26,090
She's a living person.

679
00:26:30,270 --> 00:26:31,070
Bridge piers.

680
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:32,920
The bridge piers.

681
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:34,440
Whenever I argue with her,

682
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:35,900
she would run to the river.

683
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:37,530
Let's go.

684
00:26:43,110 --> 00:26:43,790
Shuzhen!

685
00:26:44,550 --> 00:26:45,160
Mom!

686
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:47,830
Shuzhen!

687
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:52,180
Sun Lai!

688
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:57,010
Are these your mom's shoes?

689
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:58,440
My mom does have

690
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,400
a pair of shoes in this color.

691
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:00,730
Did she wear them today?

692
00:27:01,070 --> 00:27:02,070
I don't remember.

693
00:27:02,270 --> 00:27:03,240
You're so useless!

694
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,440
What do I need you for?

695
00:27:05,590 --> 00:27:06,250
Is that her?

696
00:27:06,830 --> 00:27:07,480
I think so.

697
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:10,080
Prosecutor Chen!

698
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:11,070
I can't swim.

699
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:12,440
Go... Go call for help!

700
00:27:13,550 --> 00:27:14,000
She's right there!

701
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:14,880
Okay. Alright.

702
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:15,410
Hurry up!

703
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:17,080
Don't let her drift away!

704
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,030
Shuzhen!

705
00:28:46,440 --> 00:28:48,100
Are you still feeling unwell?

706
00:28:51,240 --> 00:28:52,700
Take good care of your mom.

707
00:28:57,210 --> 00:28:57,560
Okay.

708
00:28:57,590 --> 00:28:59,320
I'm aware of the situation now.

709
00:29:00,070 --> 00:29:01,070
Prosecutor Chen.

710
00:29:03,110 --> 00:29:03,710
Thank you.

711
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:07,080
Thank you for saving our entire family.

712
00:29:07,110 --> 00:29:08,030
I also don't know why our family

713
00:29:08,030 --> 00:29:09,510
got caught up in this.

714
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:11,000
It's endless.

715
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:13,720
Today,

716
00:29:14,070 --> 00:29:16,200
I almost made you sacrifice your life.

717
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:21,860
It's fine, Mom. It's fine.

718
00:29:22,310 --> 00:29:22,910
It's fine.

719
00:29:23,510 --> 00:29:24,710
It's fine. It's fine.

720
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,160
It's fine. It's fine.

721
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:31,040
Thank you.

722
00:29:43,590 --> 00:29:44,180
Mei,

723
00:29:44,310 --> 00:29:46,440
you got a meal from the cafeteria again?

724
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:48,400
Why not go home and make some nice food?

725
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:50,260
I'm alone, so I don't want to cook.

726
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:52,510
Even if I cook, I would still eat alone.

727
00:29:52,510 --> 00:29:54,240
What a waste of time and energy.

728
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:05,510
My husband is dead.

729
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:08,840
My hometown is not in Binjiang, either.

730
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,380
Nor do I have many friends.

731
00:30:11,270 --> 00:30:12,240
My life

732
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:15,890
is probably just going to be like this.

733
00:30:29,350 --> 00:30:30,280
Have some water.

734
00:30:42,350 --> 00:30:42,920
Mei.

735
00:30:43,790 --> 00:30:45,590
I went back and thought about it.

736
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:47,220
I'll listen to you.

737
00:30:47,750 --> 00:30:48,830
Let's not return the files for now.

738
00:30:48,830 --> 00:30:51,030
We'll proceed with the trial as normal.

739
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:00,720
Xia.

740
00:31:02,510 --> 00:31:03,550
Are you serious?

741
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:06,480
Xia.

742
00:31:07,070 --> 00:31:07,880
That's great.

743
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:09,140
Well...

744
00:31:09,510 --> 00:31:10,650
W-What happened?

745
00:31:11,030 --> 00:31:12,270
Did someone persuade you?

746
00:31:12,270 --> 00:31:13,530
Was it the chief judge?

747
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:14,610
But Mei,

748
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:15,920
can we discuss it?

749
00:31:16,230 --> 00:31:18,110
By then,
let's not make a ruling immediately.

750
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,880
After the trial, let's think carefully,

751
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,070
render a decision cautiously

752
00:31:21,070 --> 00:31:22,960
and try to make it foolproof. Okay?

753
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:23,440
Okay.

754
00:31:23,830 --> 00:31:24,700
Absolutely.

755
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:25,920
If you had said this earlier,

756
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:27,920
we wouldn't have had any conflicts.

757
00:31:28,790 --> 00:31:29,270
Xia.

758
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:31,000
Thank you, Xia.

759
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:32,240
Thank you.

760
00:31:45,310 --> 00:31:46,790
When you come back from Beijing,

761
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:47,790
go to Daoxiangcun

762
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:48,980
and buy some sponge cakes

763
00:31:48,980 --> 00:31:50,160
and walnut cookies for my dad.

764
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,400
He loves those pastries.

765
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:53,400
I'm afraid I won't have enough time.

766
00:31:55,030 --> 00:31:55,440
Okay.

767
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,970
I promise I'll finish the task.

768
00:31:59,030 --> 00:32:00,160
That's more like it.

769
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:03,440
Extra points for you, silly man.

770
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:03,960
Got it.

771
00:32:05,830 --> 00:32:07,240
Have you been to Beijing before?

772
00:32:07,240 --> 00:32:08,750
I used to go there when I was a kid.

773
00:32:08,750 --> 00:32:09,880
When my dad went on business trips,

774
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:11,280
he often took me with him.

775
00:32:12,550 --> 00:32:13,410
Did you like it?

776
00:32:15,070 --> 00:32:15,730
It was okay.

777
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:19,860
Come back soon.

778
00:32:20,310 --> 00:32:21,110
Give me a kiss.

779
00:32:23,830 --> 00:32:25,090
The kids are watching.

780
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:27,880
Can't they see us?

781
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,020
No, they can't.

782
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:04,700
Have some peanuts.

783
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:05,710
Spit it out.

784
00:33:07,180 --> 00:33:08,550
I'm swamped by work here.

785
00:33:08,550 --> 00:33:09,400
It's a case, too.

786
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,860
Could you handle it for me?

787
00:33:11,830 --> 00:33:12,240
No.

788
00:33:13,830 --> 00:33:16,090
You just refused it without even asking?

789
00:33:16,230 --> 00:33:17,760
I have a lot of work to do.

790
00:33:17,790 --> 00:33:19,390
There are loads of non-litigation business
for me to handle.

791
00:33:19,390 --> 00:33:20,550
As the legal counsel for the Snail Group,

792
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:21,400
I get paid monthly in US dollars.

793
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:22,500
Don't I have to make money

794
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:24,360
to support your righteous cause?

795
00:33:24,830 --> 00:33:25,350
Lu,

796
00:33:25,930 --> 00:33:27,240
l-lawyers' lawsuits can't

797
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:28,700
just be handled for money.

798
00:33:29,480 --> 00:33:30,640
Well, you... you...

799
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:31,680
Lawyers can't

800
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:33,440
just handle lawsuits for money.

801
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:35,430
Mr. Yuan, we've already divided it up.

802
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:36,480
You're in charge of handling free cases

803
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:37,610
while I have to
take on profitable cases, right?

804
00:33:37,610 --> 00:33:39,270
This case is profitable, too.

805
00:33:40,070 --> 00:33:41,200
This case is also profitable.

806
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,130
How much is this?

807
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:43,970
200 yuan.

808
00:33:45,350 --> 00:33:46,280
200 yuan is fine.

809
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,750
A village secretary, who is also a bully,

810
00:33:47,750 --> 00:33:48,550
has been using violence

811
00:33:48,550 --> 00:33:50,510
to forcibly occupy villagers' land
for a long time.

812
00:33:50,510 --> 00:33:51,710
I won't take the case.

813
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:52,150
You...

814
00:33:52,510 --> 00:33:53,920
What's wrong with 200 yuan?

815
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:55,840
That's worth two months' salaries.

816
00:33:55,840 --> 00:33:57,440
You won't take the case, huh?

817
00:34:04,170 --> 00:34:05,140
Who paged me?

818
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:06,640
Lu, it's me.

819
00:34:08,110 --> 00:34:08,920
No wonder I've been

820
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:10,320
sneezing so much lately.

821
00:34:10,320 --> 00:34:11,110
Stop joking.

822
00:34:12,190 --> 00:34:13,190
I have a case here.

823
00:34:13,190 --> 00:34:14,050
Can you take it?

824
00:34:15,150 --> 00:34:17,030
So you're doing the same thing
as Yu Gaoyuan?

825
00:34:17,030 --> 00:34:18,290
Did he contact you too?

826
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,440
Song Xiaoguang?

827
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:20,800
No.

828
00:34:21,630 --> 00:34:23,110
Mine isn't about Song Xiaoguang.

829
00:34:23,110 --> 00:34:24,639
It's about Qian Xingliang.

830
00:34:36,510 --> 00:34:37,040
Mr. Yuan.

831
00:34:44,030 --> 00:34:45,230
Just get to the point.

832
00:34:46,510 --> 00:34:47,389
I have a case.

833
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:49,800
I'm very busy.

834
00:34:50,150 --> 00:34:51,409
I have many cases here.

835
00:34:51,710 --> 00:34:53,639
And I don't understand your cases.

836
00:34:54,030 --> 00:34:55,440
You are good at this kind of case.

837
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:57,030
What's more, it's profitable.

838
00:34:57,030 --> 00:34:57,760
This amount.

839
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:00,290
How much?

840
00:35:00,590 --> 00:35:01,250
3,000 yuan?

841
00:35:02,280 --> 00:35:02,960
Can't you be more

842
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:03,960
ambitious?

843
00:35:04,150 --> 00:35:05,020
How am I not ambitious?

844
00:35:05,020 --> 00:35:06,540
I can get 3,500 yuan here.

845
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:08,590
I can earn 3,500 yuan from my four cases.

846
00:35:08,590 --> 00:35:09,730
I-It's just 3,000 yuan,

847
00:35:09,730 --> 00:35:11,150
and you want me to handle it?

848
00:35:11,150 --> 00:35:12,590
How could you say something like that?

849
00:35:12,590 --> 00:35:14,110
You can earn 3,500 yuan
from these four cases.

850
00:35:14,110 --> 00:35:15,670
That's not even a fraction of mine.

851
00:35:15,670 --> 00:35:17,110
What do you mean
by not even a fraction of yours?

852
00:35:17,110 --> 00:35:18,360
But I have four cases.

853
00:35:18,670 --> 00:35:21,000
I can earn only 3,500 yuan
from these four cases.

854
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:23,550
What's more, each one is harder
to deal with than the last.

855
00:35:23,550 --> 00:35:24,090
What?

856
00:35:24,230 --> 00:35:25,360
Um, you have four...

857
00:35:26,030 --> 00:35:27,590
You have four cases.

858
00:35:27,610 --> 00:35:29,200
How did you do the math?

859
00:35:29,230 --> 00:35:30,710
What kind of math am I supposed to do?

860
00:35:30,710 --> 00:35:31,300
Regarding these four cases,

861
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:33,110
each one is harder
to deal with than the last.

862
00:35:33,110 --> 00:35:34,440
Over 30 migrant workers,

863
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:35,320
over 200 villagers

864
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:36,590
and a private school teacher

865
00:35:36,590 --> 00:35:37,790
are all waiting for me

866
00:35:37,960 --> 00:35:39,360
to seek justice for them.

867
00:35:39,510 --> 00:35:40,590
I'll get only 3,500 yuan.

868
00:35:40,590 --> 00:35:41,390
Is it worth it?

869
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:43,840
But you even want me
to handle this 3,000-yuan case?

870
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:45,240
Do you think I'm still...

871
00:35:45,550 --> 00:35:47,150
I'm still charging 200 yuan?

872
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:53,520
Then let me

873
00:35:54,190 --> 00:35:55,250
put it another way.

874
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:57,910
A man who has been running amok for years,

875
00:35:57,910 --> 00:35:59,440
harming dozens of women

876
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,080
and girls,

877
00:36:01,030 --> 00:36:01,510
has a powerful background

878
00:36:01,510 --> 00:36:03,550
with high-ranking officials in his family.

879
00:36:03,550 --> 00:36:05,800
With a psychiatric evaluation report,

880
00:36:05,820 --> 00:36:07,150
he can be exempt from prosecution

881
00:36:07,150 --> 00:36:08,810
and escape legal punishment.

882
00:36:08,900 --> 00:36:10,810
Millions of people in the city

883
00:36:10,850 --> 00:36:12,440
are expecting you, Mr. Yuan,

884
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:13,340
to step up and bring this

885
00:36:13,340 --> 00:36:14,600
wicked guy to justice.

886
00:36:17,150 --> 00:36:18,670
There is a western proverb.

887
00:36:18,670 --> 00:36:19,930
Laws are like cobwebs,

888
00:36:19,930 --> 00:36:22,530
which may catch small flies,
but let wasps and hornets break through.

889
00:36:22,530 --> 00:36:23,630
Mr. Yuan, do you think

890
00:36:23,630 --> 00:36:24,360
we can allow

891
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:25,130
such things

892
00:36:25,400 --> 00:36:26,230
to happen

893
00:36:26,230 --> 00:36:27,190
in our socialist China too?

894
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:28,050
Can we allow it?

895
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:30,490
Shouldn't we arrest this kind of person?

896
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:31,550
Go on.

897
00:36:32,070 --> 00:36:33,760
Do you think this case is urgent or not?

898
00:36:33,760 --> 00:36:34,820
Isn't it exciting?

899
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:37,400
Hearing what I've said, are you tempted

900
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:38,110
to take it?

901
00:36:38,590 --> 00:36:39,480
G-Go on.

902
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:40,980
What else can I say?

903
00:36:41,930 --> 00:36:42,890
A bully

904
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,480
harmed dozens of women.

905
00:36:44,510 --> 00:36:46,030
Relying on his family's background,

906
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,000
he got himself

907
00:36:47,030 --> 00:36:47,920
a psychiatric evaluation report.

908
00:36:47,920 --> 00:36:49,030
Then no one can do anything about him.

909
00:36:49,030 --> 00:36:49,560
Alright.

910
00:36:55,150 --> 00:36:56,830
H-How much is this case of yours?

911
00:36:56,830 --> 00:36:57,850
You just said mine

912
00:36:57,880 --> 00:36:58,860
is not even a fraction of yours.

913
00:36:58,860 --> 00:37:00,260
H-How much is it exactly?

914
00:37:00,960 --> 00:37:01,690
30,000 yuan.

915
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:04,770
30,000 yuan?

916
00:37:11,880 --> 00:37:12,340
Okay.

917
00:37:13,240 --> 00:37:14,320
I, Yuan Yifang, am going to

918
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:15,320
prove myself, too.

919
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:17,650
I can also earn 30,000 yuan
from a lawsuit.

920
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,680
It's not about the money.

921
00:37:21,630 --> 00:37:22,890
Justice is priceless.

922
00:37:22,960 --> 00:37:24,170
D-Don't talk about that with me.

923
00:37:24,170 --> 00:37:25,700
Go get the case files for me.

924
00:37:30,320 --> 00:37:31,070
So how many cases do I

925
00:37:31,070 --> 00:37:32,130
have to handle now?

926
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:37,250
[1988, Linshan]

927
00:37:47,900 --> 00:37:51,460
[Shaling, Xinghu, Moping]

928
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:20,160
Are you from Beijing?

929
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:25,140
You're going to Bieshan, aren't you?

930
00:38:26,400 --> 00:38:27,200
Prosecutor.

931
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:32,200
Is your name Zhang Lihui?

932
00:38:35,210 --> 00:38:36,540
That's right. Let's go.

933
00:38:36,550 --> 00:38:37,080
Let's go.

934
00:38:37,150 --> 00:38:38,880
What are you doing? Who are you?

935
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:40,000
What's your name?

936
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:41,770
Do you have your work ID?

937
00:38:42,110 --> 00:38:43,370
I'm here to pick you up.

938
00:38:44,440 --> 00:38:45,170
Your work ID.

939
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:56,040
I know you're from Beijing,

940
00:38:56,070 --> 00:38:57,440
and you're going to Bieshan.

941
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:58,670
You're a prosecutor.

942
00:39:01,590 --> 00:39:02,390
What's wrong?

943
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:04,000
So you don't trust me?

944
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:06,410
Do I look like a bad guy?

945
00:39:16,550 --> 00:39:18,670
Everyone thinks this is novel
when first arriving here.

946
00:39:18,670 --> 00:39:19,870
But after two months,

947
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:21,680
they would all clamor to go back.

948
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:22,920
After a year,

949
00:39:23,070 --> 00:39:24,400
they would all cry and shout,

950
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:27,530
"I'll never come back here again
for the rest of my life!"

951
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:29,320
Who are you talking about?

952
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:32,250
I'm talking about all the people
I've ever picked up.

953
00:39:34,550 --> 00:39:36,360
Did you offend a superior?

954
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:37,800
No.

955
00:39:38,730 --> 00:39:39,790
Did you get dumped?

956
00:39:40,110 --> 00:39:40,760
No!

957
00:39:41,710 --> 00:39:42,280
Alright.

958
00:39:42,590 --> 00:39:44,450
Then you're here for the subsidy.

959
00:39:45,110 --> 00:39:46,230
The subsidy here in Bieshan

960
00:39:46,230 --> 00:39:48,630
is indeed higher
than that in other places.

961
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,820
So you have a heavy family burden?

962
00:39:52,670 --> 00:39:55,000
I'm not married,
and I don't have a family.

963
00:39:56,290 --> 00:39:57,640
Then as a young woman,

964
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,360
why are you going to Bieshan?

965
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:00,490
For work.

966
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:02,070
For work?

967
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:05,740
There's no work there.

968
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:07,550
Everyone there is serving a sentence.

969
00:40:07,550 --> 00:40:09,550
Those who are inside the walls
are serving life sentences,

970
00:40:09,550 --> 00:40:11,400
while those who are outside the walls
are serving fixed-term sentences.

971
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:12,510
The minimum sentence is three years.

972
00:40:12,510 --> 00:40:14,280
If a person can endure it
for even two years,

973
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:15,710
then he's really tough.

974
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:19,080
Normally,
rotations are required every year.

975
00:40:22,510 --> 00:40:23,510
That prison

976
00:40:23,530 --> 00:40:25,530
actually doesn't even need guards.

977
00:40:25,670 --> 00:40:26,800
It's not necessary.

978
00:40:29,590 --> 00:40:30,150
Why?

979
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:31,470
Two years ago,

980
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:34,000
an prisoner climbed the wall and escaped.

981
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:36,110
They searched for five days and found him.

982
00:40:36,110 --> 00:40:36,710
His corpse

983
00:40:37,230 --> 00:40:39,760
was less than 500 meters
away from the prison.

984
00:40:40,110 --> 00:40:40,710
Why?

985
00:40:41,280 --> 00:40:42,410
Was his leg injured?

986
00:40:42,510 --> 00:40:43,440
He just got lost.

987
00:40:43,710 --> 00:40:44,920
It was like being trapped in a maze.

988
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:46,550
In the end, he died of thirst.

989
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,450
The soles of his shoes
were completely worn out.

990
00:40:48,450 --> 00:40:49,170
Actually,

991
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:50,710
he was just near the prison,

992
00:40:50,710 --> 00:40:52,030
walking in circles in the Gobi Desert.

993
00:40:52,030 --> 00:40:52,630
Five days,

994
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,420
500 meters.

995
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:58,330
It's fine, girl.

996
00:40:58,510 --> 00:40:59,570
Once you get there,

997
00:41:00,150 --> 00:41:02,080
just stay put and don't wander off.

998
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,360
After you endure it for three years,

999
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:07,070
you'll be able to adapt wherever you go.

1000
00:41:07,070 --> 00:41:08,320
No matter who you meet again,

1001
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:10,520
it'll just be like meeting your family.

1002
00:41:24,510 --> 00:41:25,400
Left, face!

1003
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:27,690
Double time, march!

1004
00:41:30,510 --> 00:41:31,170
Here we are.

1005
00:41:33,160 --> 00:41:35,050
[The Procuratorate Office‌ in Bieshan Prison,
Xijiang Province Bieshan Prison]

1006
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:44,190
Thanks for your hard work.

1007
00:41:44,190 --> 00:41:45,840
Thanks for coming all this way.

1008
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:46,300
Mr. Guo.

1009
00:41:47,050 --> 00:41:47,840
I've brought her here for you.

1010
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:48,570
You can check.

1011
00:41:48,570 --> 00:41:50,230
Not a single piece is missing.

1012
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:53,090
He didn't scare you on the way, did he?

1013
00:41:53,160 --> 00:41:54,450
He always tells others

1014
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:55,570
that an escaped prisoner

1015
00:41:55,570 --> 00:41:57,500
ran five kilometers in three days.

1016
00:41:57,870 --> 00:41:59,730
Wasn't it 500 meters in five days?

1017
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:02,550
You brat!

1018
00:42:02,840 --> 00:42:04,570
You haven't changed, have you?

1019
00:42:06,450 --> 00:42:07,450
This is Mr. Guo.

1020
00:42:07,630 --> 00:42:09,320
You guys got three years' imprisonment.

1021
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:10,550
He got life imprisonment.

1022
00:42:10,550 --> 00:42:10,920
Shoo!

1023
00:42:11,710 --> 00:42:12,840
My name's Guo Dajie.

1024
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:15,110
I'm a resident prosecutor here.

1025
00:42:15,110 --> 00:42:17,370
I've been working here for over 20 years.

1026
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:19,260
These brats always make fun of me,

1027
00:42:19,770 --> 00:42:21,830
saying that I got life imprisonment.

1028
00:42:22,520 --> 00:42:23,440
Zhang, right?

1029
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:25,180
Zhang... Zhang Lihui.

1030
00:42:25,280 --> 00:42:25,550
Yes.

1031
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:26,370
Welcome.

1032
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:28,230
Hello, Mentor.

1033
00:42:28,230 --> 00:42:29,690
Hello. Don't call me that.

1034
00:42:29,790 --> 00:42:32,190
Don't call me Mentor.
Just call me Comrade.

1035
00:42:32,190 --> 00:42:32,790
Thank you.

1036
00:42:33,440 --> 00:42:35,500
Here are the documents and medicine.

1037
00:42:35,770 --> 00:42:36,770
Okay, okay, okay.

1038
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:38,110
Please don't mind it.

1039
00:42:38,110 --> 00:42:39,440
Just stay here tonight.

1040
00:42:39,760 --> 00:42:40,800
I don't want to spend a night

1041
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:41,460
in a prison.

1042
00:42:41,790 --> 00:42:43,000
I'm going back to the town.

1043
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:43,670
Okay.

1044
00:42:43,900 --> 00:42:44,720
Just go.

1045
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:45,710
Alright.

1046
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:46,110
Miss,

1047
00:42:46,590 --> 00:42:47,190
take care.

1048
00:42:47,630 --> 00:42:48,810
Drive safely.

1049
00:42:49,030 --> 00:42:49,360
Okay.

1050
00:42:49,630 --> 00:42:50,160
Alright.

1051
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:50,980
Give it to me.

1052
00:42:50,980 --> 00:42:51,630
I can carry it myself.

1053
00:42:51,630 --> 00:42:52,560
Just give it to me.

1054
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:53,150
I'll hold it for you.

1055
00:42:53,150 --> 00:42:53,960
-Give it to me.
-Thanks, Mentor.

1056
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:54,490
Let's go.

1057
00:42:54,520 --> 00:42:55,720
Don't call me Mentor.

1058
00:42:57,150 --> 00:42:57,680
Let's go.

1059
00:42:57,880 --> 00:42:58,760
Come on in. Come on.
